Vendored third-party dependency, moved to soroban-sdk 29
========================================================

  Library:  admin-sep 0.28.1 (Rust, no_std)
  Upstream: https://github.com/theahaco/admin-sep
  Release:  crates.io admin-sep 0.28.1 (.crate sha256
            c0964ae3e1b37e70d3839ad3fb2f17b1f2287bdac3c188a3434985a7d0d37bf7),
            published from commit 418df961f16d8d2857578f3d22d1a2a79458ee57
            ("chore: release v0.28.1 (#20)"), path admin_sep
  License:  Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE)
  Used by:  perch-stateless-registry (`Administratable`, `Upgradable`)

Why vendored
------------
admin-sep 0.28.1, its newest release, requires soroban-sdk ^28, and no
upstream branch moves it to 29 (checked 2026-11-03). Its only source changes
from 0.27.0, the release perch used before, are the soroban-sdk 28
migration: `set_admin` and `upgrade` take their argument by reference, and
`upgrade` calls `update_current_contract(ContractExecutable::Wasm(..))`,
which invokes the same host function as `update_current_contract_wasm`.
Perch builds with soroban-sdk 29.0.1 / soroban-env-host 29.0.1, and a crate
that requires another soroban-sdk major cannot share its types, so this copy
is built as a path dependency with the soroban-sdk pin moved. No change was
proposed upstream.

Upstream files
--------------
Every file is upstream's bytes except Cargo.toml (the published, normalized
manifest), whose delta is below. UPSTREAM.sha256 lists the sha256 of every
vendored file as published, with LICENSE taken from the repository root at
the commit above (the published crate carries none).

Not vendored: Cargo.lock, Cargo.toml.orig, rust-toolchain.toml.

SDK 29 delta
------------
Cargo.toml only:

  - `[dependencies.soroban-sdk]` version "28.0.0" became "29.0.1";
  - the `[dev-dependencies]` table was dropped.

The source builds unchanged: soroban-sdk 29 has no API changes from 28
(soroban-sdk's own migration notes: "Migrating from v28 to v29: None").

Updating
--------
Replace the directory with the new upstream files, re-apply the delta above,
regenerate UPSTREAM.sha256 from the unmodified upstream files, and update
this NOTICE. crates/integration-tests/tests/vendor.rs requires every
vendored file other than Cargo.toml to hash to UPSTREAM.sha256 (after
reversing any source delta above) and the directory to hold nothing else but
NOTICE and UPSTREAM.sha256, so no other upstream byte can change unnoticed.
